{
  "dom_id": "step-q279379",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The vector $v=\u27e8-\\sqrt{2},\\,\\,2\\sqrt{3}\u27e9$ is rotated $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin. Find the image of $v$ under this rotation.\n\n${v}^{\u2032}=\u27e8$ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "A rotation of $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ radians *clockwise* about the origin is represented by the matrix \n\n$$\n{R}_{(-5\\pi /4)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image ${v}^{\u2032}$ under the action of the matrix ${R}_{(-5\\pi /4)}$, we compute the matrix product, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{\u2032} & ={R}_{(-5\\pi /4)}\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\sqrt{6} \\\\ -1-\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image is ${v}^{\u2032}=\u27e81-\\sqrt{6},-1-\\sqrt{6}\u27e9.$",
